  <article class="tp-article">

  <div class="tp-answer" id="quick-answer"><p><strong>Quick answer:</strong> adults need about <strong>25&nbsp;g of fiber a day (women)</strong> and <strong>38&nbsp;g (men)</strong> up to age 50, and 21&nbsp;g and 30&nbsp;g after 50. Another rule is 14&nbsp;g per 1,000 calories. Most Americans eat only about 15&nbsp;g.</p></div>

